= V1 ontology maturation =

This audit applies the [[BITwiki:V1 to V2 maturation|V1 → V2 maturation sequence]] to ontology and classification:

'''preserve → understand → identify signal → mature primitive → enhance → integrate.'''

The purpose is not to decide whether V1's ontology was "right" or "wrong." V1 contains several overlapping models developed through experimentation. The task is to identify the durable functions inside those models, distinguish them from implementation reality, and express them through coherent V2 primitives.

== Evidence boundary ==

This audit distinguishes three evidence layers:

# '''Archived implementation''' — namespaces, pages, revisions, semantic annotations, category memberships, template callers, and other objects preserved in <code>archive-v1/</code>.
# '''V1 design writings''' — ontology, taxonomy, page-type, entity-type, relationship, property, and interoperability specifications, whether or not their proposed machinery was instantiated.
# '''Current V2 architecture''' — the source-reconciled semantic model in [[BITwiki:Ontology]], [[BITwiki:Entity types]], [[BITwiki:Relationships]], [[BITwiki:Semantic properties]], [[Property:Entity type]], [[Property:Domain]], Categories, Portals, and related standards.

A proposal in layer 2 is design evidence, not proof of implementation in layer 1.

